  "fire": {
    "launch_frame": 2,
    "spawn_frame": 4,
    "index_deg": 120,
    "frames": 32,
    "recoil_m": 0.01,
    "recoil_frames": [
      15,
      15
    ],
    "note": "fire always starts from rest: the top tube (Tube1) fires. On frame 2 the kick charge fires (muzzle flash at Muzzle1, backblast at Backblast) and Tube1 starts its recoil: 1 cm back into the drum in 15 frames and home in 15. The loaded rocket (bone LoadedRocket) runs up the tube and is scaled to nothing on frame 4: spawn the projectile then at Muzzle1's transform (its tail on the gizmo, facing its forward) and play its deploy. Meanwhile the lock withdraws, the drum indexes 120 deg clockwise (seen by the gunner; the pinion -360 deg) and relocks. The drum is three-fold symmetric and the gear pair ends on whole teeth, so the next fire can start from rest again (the next tube is then Tube1): play fire once per shot. Each tube is its own slide bone (Tube1..Tube3) if the game wants to track the drum itself."
  },
